=== SURVEY ===
Current `HybridLiveSignalStore.Warm` behavior (live_store.go:229-247):
  1. Validates ctx and vehicleID.
  2. Returns nil immediately if `redisCache()` is nil (mode != hybrid
     OR no L2 wired). This is the "Redis disabled / L2 absent" no-op
     path and MUST remain unchanged after Prompt 06.
  3. Calls `l2.GetAllValues(ctx, vehicleID)`. Wraps any error as
     `"warm live signals from Redis for vehicle %d: %w"` and returns.
     This is the only error path Warm currently has, and Prompt 06's
     restamp MUST surface its errors through the same return path
     (no new error sentinel, no panic, no swallowed error).
  4. Calls `s.hydrateMissingValues(vehicleID, values)` and returns
     nil on success.

Current `hydrateMissingValues` behavior (live_store.go:263-288):
  - Acquires `s.l1.mu.Lock()` for the duration of the hydration so
    L1 is updated atomically.
  - Iterates the Redis values map. For each entry:
      * Skips when `value == nil || value.Raw == nil` (deleted /
        unparseable — must remain a skip after restamp).
      * Skips when `value.Timestamp.IsZero()` — THIS IS THE GAP that
        Prompt 06 must close. After restamp, these entries no longer
        have zero timestamps because they were rewritten via Update,
        so this skip naturally becomes a no-op for legacy data.
      * Skips when an L1 entry already exists (live wins — preserved).
      * Otherwise clones the Redis value into L1 via cloneSignalValue.

Current `RedisSignalCache.Update` behavior (redis_cache.go:65-109):
  - Encodes every non-nil, non-`{invalid:true}` value via
    `encodeTimestampedSignalValue(val, time.Now().UTC())` →
    teslasync.signal.v1 envelope JSON containing
    `{encoding, value, legacy_value, timestamp, source}`.
  - Writes all fields in a single variadic HSET round-trip on
    `vehicle:{vehicleID}:signals`.
  - Refreshes the key TTL to `signalKeyTTL` (7 * 24h) via EXPIRE.
  - Confirms restamp can be implemented by simply calling
    `Update(ctx, vehicleID, restampPayload)` — no new encoder, no
    new envelope, no schema change, no new Redis key/channel.

Therefore the restamp algorithm Prompt 06 must implement is:
  a. After `GetAllValues`, identify entries whose Timestamp is zero
     AND whose Raw is non-nil (legacy scalars only).
  b. Build a `map[string]interface{}` of {name → Raw} for those
     entries only (envelope entries are never copied into the
     restamp payload — they keep their original timestamp byte-for-
     byte).
  c. Call `cache.Update(ctx, vehicleID, restampPayload)` so the
     existing envelope encoder, TTL refresh, and HSET round-trip
     are reused unchanged.
  d. Re-read the cache (or update the local `values` map in place
     with the rewritten Raw + new Timestamp) and pass the result
     to `hydrateMissingValues` so L1 is now hydrated for the
     previously-skipped legacy fields.
The contract is "Warm rewrites legacy scalars as envelopes with a
synthetic time.Now() timestamp, preserves their values bit-for-bit,
never deletes a field, never overwrites a fresh envelope, and is
safe to retry."

=== REASONING ===
Restamp contract clauses (each maps 1:1 to a test case in CHANGES):

  R1 (value preserved bit-for-bit). The restamp path MUST round-trip
      the Raw value. A legacy scalar `"100"` decodes to float64(100)
      via `decodeLegacySignalValue`; after restamp + GetAllValues, the
      Raw value MUST still be float64(100) (number stays number).
      Likewise `"true"` → bool(true) → bool(true), and a non-numeric
      string (e.g. a JSON object literal preserved as-is) round-trips
      without coercion. No precision loss, no type widening, no
      string fallback for values that decoded as numbers/bools.

  R2 (only legacy entries restamped). The restamp path MUST stamp
      ONLY entries whose Timestamp is zero. Entries that already
      carry a non-zero envelope timestamp MUST NOT be re-encoded
      (their Timestamp would otherwise jump forward to time.Now()
      and falsely pass the 2-minute freshness threshold). The
      discriminator is the value returned by GetAllValues, NOT a
      regex over the raw HSET string — Prompt 06 MUST inspect
      `value.Timestamp.IsZero()` and skip the entry from the
      restamp payload when it is false.

  R3 (idempotent / safe to retry). After Warm completes, every
      entry in the hash carries a non-zero Timestamp. A second Warm
      call MUST detect zero legacy entries to restamp and either
      issue zero writes (preferred) or issue an idempotent rewrite
      that does not change the value field. The first option is
      strongly preferred because it keeps the restamp Update call
      payload empty and avoids touching TTL twice unnecessarily.
      Either way, the value field MUST be preserved bit-for-bit
      across the second call.

  R4 (partial-failure safe). If `GetAllValues` returns an error,
      Warm MUST surface it via the existing wrapped return path
      (no panic, no L1 mutation). If Update on the restamp payload
      returns an error mid-run, the implementation MUST NOT have
      DEL'd any field beforehand and MUST NOT retry indefinitely;
      the partially-restamped state in Redis is acceptable so long
      as no field was deleted or had its value corrupted (the
      remaining legacy entries can be restamped on the next Warm
      call). The error MUST be surfaced through Warm's return.

  R5 (L1 hydrated after restamp). Today, legacy entries are skipped
      in hydrateMissingValues because of `Timestamp.IsZero()`. After
      restamp those same entries now carry a non-zero Timestamp and
      MUST flow through hydrateMissingValues into L1. Verification
      anchors: `LocalVehicleIDs()` includes the warmed vehicle, and
      `s.l1.Get(vehicleID, name)` returns a non-nil Value with the
      preserved Raw. Live-wins is preserved: any L1 entry that
      already existed before Warm MUST NOT be overwritten by the
      restamped Redis entry (the existing skip-when-exists branch
      handles this and MUST remain).

  R6 (TTL refreshed). The restamp Update call MUST refresh the
      7-day TTL on `vehicle:{vehicleID}:signals` because it goes
      through `RedisSignalCache.Update`, which already runs EXPIRE
      with `signalKeyTTL` after every HSET. The test asserts that
      after Warm, the EXPIRE call was issued (instrumented via the
      fakeRedisSignalClient). This is also the implicit guarantee
      that no separate TTL handling code path is introduced — the
      restamp path MUST NOT bypass Update.

  R7 (no key/channel rename, no field deletion). The restamp MUST
      use the existing key `vehicle:{vehicleID}:signals` and MUST
      NOT issue HDEL or DEL. Existing fields that are not in the
      restamp payload (i.e. the fresh envelope entries skipped per
      R2) MUST remain in the hash with their original byte content.
      This preserves backwards compatibility for any not-yet-
      upgraded reader pod (per ADR-007 / instructions).

Test scope decision: the new tests MUST live in
`internal/signal/live_store_test.go` (package signal — internal tests)
so they can reach `s.l1` and the unexported `hydrateMissingValues`
helper as needed for R5 verification, and so they can reuse the
existing `fakeRedisSignalClient` and `redisSignalKey(vehicleID)`
helpers without duplicating fixtures.

